 broken by design until later stages wire its open rows. Its Error List was read in full (65 items, down from 83), and the expected-errors file matches. STATUS `current-bed:` now points to it.\n\n- **Wrong claim at the start:** cycle 112 had written that the tools for B2b already existed. The first card (113-1) found, without opening LabVIEW, that 3 of the 9 rows had no wiring route. That was my fault as judgement.\n- **Wiring tool added:** card 113-2 extended `tools/stagexec.py` so a front-panel control or indicator can be wired to a loop tunnel's outer face. It passed a live check on a copy of the working VI (20 of 20 checks) and its own self-test (124 of 124). All 9 rows then had a route.\n- **First launch stopped before saving:** Build Array `#11261` renamed its input from 'array' to 'element' once row b2_03 was wired. Its other input, `t11273`, is left open for the later queue-transport stage (QRT), and no row in this stage wires it. Nothing was saved.\n- **Decision (PD227(d)):** row b2_03 moves to the stage that wires `t11273`, so both inputs of that Build Array are wired together. The two candidate causes were not measured; there is no reader for the relevant Build Array setting or for terminal data types. The decision holds under either cause. The second launch, with the other 8 rows, passed 26 of 26 checks and saved the file.\n- **Retrospective:** it named one fault: this is the same Build Array rename that hit `#2626` in cycle 110, and I did not have the plan step check for it. It cost about 24 minutes and the cycle's last allowed retry. I accepted it and recorded a tool decision in `docs/violation-decisions.md` (02:25). Cycle 114 first builds an offline pre-run check that flags a row wiring one Build Array input while another input is still open. It must flag exactly `#2626` and `#11261` on the old plans.\n- **The earlier overdue warning** (reasoning instead of measuring, 28 occurrences) is answered with a \"no new tool\" decision, because the toward-S1 check from cycle 112 already enforces it in code.\n\n**Next (`tools/bench/next.json`, validated; STATUS `## NEXT`):** cycle 114 builds that pre-run check first, then stage L2-B3 (rows B3-01..06) from the new working VI. All 6 rows get a route check with LabVIEW closed before any script is written, then one launch.\n\nTwo small bookkeeping bugs are carried, not fixed:\n- the retry-launch log recorded `card=None` even though the retry card was on the command;\n- the launch guard refuses the argument order that the new build script's own comment gives.\n\nSTATUS.md is now 414 lines against its ~100-line limit and needs trimming in a later documentation pass. No questions are open for you from this cycle.","ttft_ms":2063,"type":"result","duration_ms":5500897,"uuid":"157398b6-ecb4-46bf-8914-4c83922600de","ttft_stream_ms":1871,"time_to_request_ms":225,"first_content_frame_ms":1871,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
